# cylinder_bore_inch.cam — the K1 slice-1 acceptance fixture (DECISIONS.md
# "K1 slice 1 — the formatting boundary…"): cylinder_bore_arcs.cam's exact
# program — mm-authored, mm-modeled — on a DECLARED inch machine. The golden
# says G20 where the mm twin says G21, every X/Y/Z/I/J word at 4 inch
# decimals (50mm → X1.9685), every F word at the machine's declared 2
# (800mm/min → F31.50), and the S words byte-identical to the twin's —
# conversion changes numbers, never structure, and never a unit-free word.
# compress=arcs is chosen deliberately so the golden proves the arc IJ words
# convert with the coordinates they steer; the control-comp run proves the
# G41/D lines and the tool-header D-register value (what the operator DIALS)
# speak inch too.
machine shop_inch.machine

units mm
feed 800
plunge 300
rapid_z 5
clearance_z 25
spindle 3000

stock Box(w=100, l=100, h=20, x=0, y=0, z=0)

tool T5 Endmill(dia=10.0)

feature Bore CylinderBore(dia=40.0, extent=12.0, x=50.0, y=50.0)

run Side(tool=T5, surface=Bore, stepover=5.0, compress=arcs)
run Side(tool=T5, surface=Bore, stepover=5.0, comp=control, compress=arcs)
